reply-writer Repository Version History
=======================================

v1.0.3 (Release Date: TBD)
--------------------------
- Clarify policy governance, pull request scope and automated agent workflows.
- Reject surrounding whitespace in generation base URLs before API requests.
- Report reply delivery and input restoration accurately on error pages.
- Handle CLI draft output failures without exposing exception details.
- Preserve safe request diagnostics and exclude untrusted API metadata from
  logs.
- Parse integer settings exactly without floating-point rounding.
- Classify excessively nested generated JSON as an invalid response.
- Refuse generation API redirects to keep input on the configured endpoint.
- Show live character counts in retry and regeneration forms.

v1.0.2 (2026-09-21)
-------------------
- Align CLI overrides with config.py's normalization: fix --model/--prompt-dir
  blank handling and move --timeout's validity check into config.py.
- Validate prompt sets before generation, including multiline double-brace
  forms, so required placeholders occur once and unknown forms are refused.
- Reject using standard input for both CLI message and direction.
- Frame prompt inputs with collision-free request boundaries, keeping received
  messages data and directions limited to reply-writing instructions.
- Reject malformed endpoint hosts, ports and embedded whitespace before
  generation, keep LOG_LEVEL's INFO fallback robust and document limits.
- Keep missing information from creating a future undertaking absent from input.
- Add GENERATION_OUTPUT_TOKEN_PARAMETER so MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS can use
  max_tokens or max_completion_tokens without endpoint guessing.
- Show live message/direction counts, match server limits to textarea length,
  and add Generating feedback with duplicate-submit suppression.
- Refuse non-UTF-8 CLI inputs and prompt files without exposing a traceback.
- Log failures once at entry points without raw exception, file-error or
  client-request path text.
- Require a usable finish reason before accepting a generation response.
- Make the Procfile use port 8091 when PORT is unset.
- Refuse non-standard NaN and Infinity constants in generated JSON responses.
- Refuse unknown response modes in the provider before sending a request.

